A||||3||BN Boomer||Headlight swapping||||5||
Z||000000||BN Boomer||04-06-2000||09:58 PM||||I'm trying to swap the headlight assemblies and wiring harness out of my wrecked 87 Coupe into my one-eyed 85 GT. I would like to just swap the harnesses to avoid having to splice things together. Removing the light assemblies themselves, the module, and most of the wiring harness was easy enough, but how do you get the harness out of the front where it runs underneath the metal in front of the radiator? Please don't tell me I have to remove the hood and nose. Is this going to be more trouble than it's worth? <P>Ogre, I recall you saying not so long ago that this was not a difficult task, just time consuming. Any suggestions? I don't mind spinning wrenches, just don't like doing so unnecessarilly.<P>Also, the control module was mounted between the firewall and fender in the 87. Would it be okay to just mount it somewhere out of the way inside the headlight compartment itself on the 85?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-07-2000||08:55 AM||||haven't dug into the front that far. I don't know how far apart you have to pull things to get it out.<P>Unless you are sure the controller and connectors are water tight I'd keep it some place in the spare tire well. Besides, the area around the radiator gets Hot. probly not good for it either.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HarryG||04-07-2000||03:27 PM||||When I got an '87 harness from the boneyard last summer, I was able to get that part free by pulling off the plastic sleeve and slipping 1 or 2 wires at a time through the opening. Before I figured this out, I think I took off the hood, Can't remember whether that was actually needed or not!  ||||reg||3
Z||000003||BN Boomer||04-08-2000||06:32 PM||||UPDATE:<P>For anyone interested, you need to remove the hood in order to remove the headlight wiring harness intact. Once the hood is off, the harness itself can be fished out from in front of the radiator and if you are able to find a break in the corrugated plastic sleaving, the wires themselves can be worked out between the very close clearance points near the mounts for the hood. ||||reg||10
